# Deliberately divergent oracle — NOT part of the committed passing corpus.
#
# Real Bitty divergence: mode ?47 switches the alternate buffer but does not
# save/restore the cursor. xterm's cursor is global across a buffer switch
# (charproc.c `srm_ALTBUF`: no CursorSave/CursorRestore, unlike 1049) and
# ghostty's SwitchScreenMode .@"47" copies the cursor both directions, so
# "X ?47h Y ?47l Z" in the reference leaves Z at column 2 -> row "X Z" and
# cursor column 3. Bitty's `switch_alt_screen` saves/restores the cursor for
# Via47 too, leaving "XZ" and cursor column 2. The expectation below records
# the reference behaviour the runner disagrees with.
area: alternate-screen
provenance: capture|xterm patch #411 charproc.c srm_ALTBUF + ghostty SwitchScreenMode .@"47"
grid: 80x24
grid_text: unchecked
row 0: X Z
cursor: 0 3 visible
